Mark patched builds in the PHP version string

Appends "-elife-CVE-2026-109618-109619" to PHP_EXTRA_VERSION, so it shows up in
`php -v`, PHP_VERSION/phpversion() and phpinfo(). PHP_VERSION_ID is unchanged (70433).

Patches the generated configure script (not configure.ac): the build doesn't run
buildconf, and main/php_version.h is regenerated by configure.

Update the suffix when patches in this directory are added or removed.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3830,7 +3830,7 @@
 PHP_MAJOR_VERSION=$1
 PHP_MINOR_VERSION=$2
 PHP_RELEASE_VERSION=$3
-PHP_EXTRA_VERSION=$4
+PHP_EXTRA_VERSION="$4-elife-CVE-2026-109618-109619"
 PHP_VERSION="$PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.$PHP_MINOR_VERSION.$PHP_RELEASE_VERSION$PHP_EXTRA_VERSION"
 PHP_VERSION_ID=`expr $PHP_MAJOR_VERSION \* 10000 + $PHP_MINOR_VERSION \* 100 + $PHP_RELEASE_VERSION`
 
